{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6gwen3uQJs2zWoTkQeM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Analysis Summary\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd the ability for customers to cancel orders with a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that manages order and shipment statuses atomically, with idempotent retry safety and all-or-nothing semantics when conflicts exist.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model: `Order.kt:11` — currently no status field\n- Shipment model: `Shipment.kt:9` — already has `ShipmentStatus` enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt:16` — implements create/get endpoints\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:22` — implements create/get endpoints  \n- ApiExceptions: `ApiExceptions.kt:11` — base exception hierarchy with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31` — closed set of error codes\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. **Error handling:** Uses sealed `ApiException` subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) paired with `ErrorCode` enum; GlobalExceptionHandler centralizes response formatting\n2. **HTTP status:** CREATED (201) for successful POST, OK (200) for GET, CONFLICT (409) for state conflicts, NOT_FOUND (404) for missing resources\n3. **Tests:** MockMvc with jsonPath assertions; @BeforeEach clears repository state\n4. **Data models:** Immutable Kotlin data classes\n5. **Repository pattern:** In-memory stores using ConcurrentHashMap; find methods return List or nullable types\n6. **Error responses:** Wrapped in `ApiError` envelope with code, message, fields\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — add `status: OrderStatus` field; new orders default to ACTIVE\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` — add `findByOrderId` method (required for shipment lookups)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add `findByOrderId` method (required to find shipments to cancel)\n4. `OrderController.kt` — add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — gate `POST /shipments` to reject when order is CANCELLED\n6. `ApiError.kt` — add error codes for the new rejection cases\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for all cancel cases (active → cancelled, idempotent retry, conflict with CONFIRMED shipment, missing order, create shipment on cancelled order)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. **Atomicity:** The in-memory store with ConcurrentHashMap doesn't guarantee transaction-like atomicity across reads and writes; if a shipment status changes between checking and canceling, the constraint could be violated. However, the test environment is single-threaded, so this is acceptable for the fixture.\n2. **Idempotency:** Must ensure a second cancel of an already-CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing.\n3. **All-or-nothing:** If a shipment transitions to CONFIRMED between the check and the cancel, the order could be partially updated. The specification requires rejecting the entire operation if any shipment is already CONFIRMED at decision time.\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — all cases are specified, including the all-or-nothing constraint, idempotent retry, 404 for missing order, and 409 for creating shipments on cancelled orders.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**\n   - Add `status: OrderStatus` field (non-optional, defaults to ACTIVE in creation)\n   - Add new `OrderStatus` enum with values ACTIVE and CANCELLED\n   - Update `CreateOrderRequest` (no change — status is not user-provided at creation)\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**\n   - Add method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` that queries ShipmentRepository (requires dependency injection)\n   - Alternatively, add a `findShipmentsByOrderId` helper that the repository can use by filtering its internal store\n   - Decision: Inject ShipmentRepository and query directly from OrderRepository\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**\n   - Add public method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to retrieve all shipments for a given order\n\n4. **OrderController.kt**\n   - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint\n   - Logic:\n     - Throw ResourceNotFoundException if order does not exist\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return 200 OK with the order (idempotent)\n     - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException and abort (all-or-nothing)\n     - Change order status to CANCELLED\n     - For each CREATED shipment, change status to CANCELLED\n     - Persist changes\n     - Return 200 OK with the cancelled order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**\n   - Modify `create` endpoint to:\n     - Check if the order exists and has status CANCELLED\n     - If yes, throw ConflictException with code ORDER_CANCELLED\n     - If order doesn't exist, proceed (order may be created later — \"keeps its current behaviour\")\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**\n   - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code (for shipments being created on a cancelled order)\n   - Add `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` error code (for cancels blocked by confirmed shipments)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**\n   - Test 1: Cancel an ACTIVE order with no shipments → 200 OK, order is CANCELLED\n   - Test 2: Cancel an ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments → 200 OK, order and all CREATED shipments are CANCELLED\n   - Test 3: Cancel an order that is already CANCELLED → 200 OK, nothing changes (idempotent)\n   - Test 4: Cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment → 409 CONFLICT with code ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n   - Test 5: Cancel an order that does not exist → 404 NOT_FOUND\n   - Test 6: Create a shipment on a CANCELLED order → 409 CONFLICT with code ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Alternative approaches considered and rejected:**\n\n1. **Use a service layer for cancel logic**\n   - Rejected: Existing codebase has no service layer; logic lives in controllers. Staying consistent with existing patterns reduces surface area for errors.\n\n2. **Store shipment-to-order index in OrderRepository**\n   - Rejected: Would require maintaining a bidirectional index, adding complexity. ShipmentRepository already has all shipments; filtering by orderId is simple.\n\n3. **Make cancel idempotent by using a dedicated cancel method rather than setting status directly**\n   - Rejected: Status field is sufficient; setting CANCELLED on an already-CANCELLED order is a no-op as long as we don't re-cancel the shipments (which we won't because the order status is already CANCELLED).\n\n4. **Check shipment confirmations at response time rather than decision time**\n   - Rejected: Violates the all-or-nothing constraint; if a shipment becomes CONFIRMED between check and update, the contract is broken.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order (no shipments) | Order, shipments list | Order.status → CANCELLED | 200 OK, order | OrderController, persist via repository |\n| Cancel ACTIVE order (CREATED shipments) | Order, shipments list | Order.status → CANCELLED, Shipment.status → CANCELLED for each CREATED | 200 OK, order | OrderController, persist via repository |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | Order, shipments list | (nothing) | 200 OK, order | OrderController, idempotent check |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | Order, shipments list | (nothing, abort) | 409 CONFLICT, ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT | ConflictException, GlobalExceptionHandler formats error |\n| Cancel missing order | (not found) | (nothing) | 404 NOT_FOUND, ORDER_NOT_FOUND | ResourceNotFoundException, GlobalExceptionHandler formats error |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | Order, check status | (nothing, abort) | 409 CONFLICT, ORDER_CANCELLED | ConflictException, GlobalExceptionHandler formats error |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Cancel ACTIVE order with no shipments**\n   - Setup: Create order O-1\n   - Action: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n   - Assert: 200 OK, response body has status=CANCELLED, GET /orders/O-1 confirms CANCELLED\n\n2. **Test: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments**\n   - Setup: Create order O-2, create shipment S-1 for O-2 with status CREATED\n   - Action: POST /orders/O-2/cancel\n   - Assert: 200 OK, order O-2 is CANCELLED, GET /shipments/S-1 shows status CANCELLED\n\n3. **Test: Cancel already-CANCELLED order (idempotent retry)**\n   - Setup: Create order O-3, cancel it once (POST /orders/O-3/cancel → 200 OK)\n   - Action: POST /orders/O-3/cancel again\n   - Assert: 200 OK, order O-3 still CANCELLED, nothing else changed\n\n4. **Test: Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment (all-or-nothing)**\n   - Setup: Create order O-4, create shipment S-2 for O-4, manually set S-2.status = CONFIRMED\n   - Action: POST /orders/O-4/cancel\n   - Assert: 409 CONFLICT with code ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, GET /orders/O-4 shows status ACTIVE (unchanged), GET /shipments/S-2 shows status CONFIRMED (unchanged)\n\n5. **Test: Cancel non-existent order**\n   - Setup: (none)\n   - Action: POST /orders/O-missing/cancel\n   - Assert: 404 NOT_FOUND with code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n6. **Test: Create shipment on CANCELLED order**\n   - Setup: Create order O-5, cancel it (POST /orders/O-5/cancel → 200 OK)\n   - Action: POST /shipments with orderId=O-5\n   - Assert: 409 CONFLICT with code ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":21568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d568ecb-f5ca-4a72-980c-19dd0eec9c73","uuid":"f36f2d8f-5e6f-48e8-b895-fed13491fb1f","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:02:42.069Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6gwdnGGQL3BVSRHLwgF"}
